    "q-253542": {
      "dom_id": "step-q253542",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "What is the infimum of the set $C=\\{-1,\\,-3,\\,0,\\,2,\\,1,\\,-2\\}?$\n\n$inf(C)=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "The infimum of a set $C$ is the greatest lower bound of $C.$\n\nIf $C$ is a finite set, the infimum of $C$ equals its minimum. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}inf(C) & =min\\{-1,\\,-3,\\,0,\\,2,\\,1,\\,-2\\}=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
